+ # OpenClaw Beta 8 Update Audit - 2026-05-14
+ ## Scope
+ Updated and audited three remote macOS OpenClaw installs against `2026.5.12-beta.8` (`097daf9`) using:
+ ```sh
+ openclaw update --channel beta --tag 2026.5.12-beta.8 --yes --timeout 1800
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ One install was reported down before this run after an earlier operator-attempted beta 8 update. Host identifiers, usernames, IPs, channel/account identifiers, local personal paths, tokens, session ids, and private prompt/workspace content are intentionally omitted or generalized.
+ The upstream tag was present at `refs/tags/v2026.5.12-beta.8` with SHA `1859eab1bf64fe6e37fdc89ea1eb4e2210a7bf42`.
+ ## Starting Versions
+ - Host A: `2026.5.12-beta.5`
+ - Host B: `2026.5.12-beta.4`
+ - Host C: `2026.5.12-beta.5`; gateway initially not reachable even though its LaunchAgent was loaded.
+ ## Update Result
+ All three installs now report:
+ - `openclaw --version`: `OpenClaw 2026.5.12-beta.8 (097daf9)`
+ - `openclaw update status`: up to date on npm beta `2026.5.12-beta.8`
+ - `openclaw gateway status --deep`: LaunchAgent loaded, gateway running, connectivity probe OK, CLI version and gateway version both `2026.5.12-beta.8`
+ Two hosts updated smoothly through the normal updater flow:
+ - Host A updated from beta 5 to beta 8 in about 51 seconds.
+ - Host B updated from beta 4 to beta 8 in about 47 seconds.
+ - Post-update direct non-delivered agent checks succeeded on both with `openai/gpt-5.5`, `agentHarnessId: codex`, and `fallbackUsed: false`.
+ The previously down host required service repair after the package/plugin update completed:
+ - The beta 8 package and plugin update completed, but the restart phase failed while refreshing the gateway LaunchAgent.
+ - The gateway binary could start in the foreground, but launchd kept terminating the managed gateway shortly after readiness.
+ - A stale submitted launchd updater job was repeatedly exiting with code `127` and triggering gateway termination. Removing that submitted updater job and restarting the gateway restored stable service.
+ - The LaunchAgent was temporarily rewritten to run Node directly with inline environment variables because macOS logs showed policy friction around the generated service-env wrapper script. Token values were not copied into this report.
+ - Channels are connected again after repair: Discord connected, Telegram connected, WhatsApp linked/running/connected.
+ - Direct agent routing on this host still needs operator attention: the check fell back to an embedded Anthropic/PI route because the Codex/OpenAI OAuth token refresh returned `401 token_expired`.
+ ## Maintainer-Facing Bugs/Issues
+ Filed/updated upstream:
+ - Stale updater-process warning continuation: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/81394#issuecomment-4452641406
+ - `lossless-claw` stale config / `plugins doctor` continuation: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/81499#issuecomment-4452643184
+ - New launchd/update-job gateway loop issue: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/81859
+ ### 1. Submitted updater launchd job can survive/loop and keep killing the gateway
+ On the host that was down before this run, the update package step completed but the gateway did not remain online. The managed gateway repeatedly reached readiness and then received `SIGTERM` a few seconds later.
+ Sanitized evidence:
+ Sanitized evidence:
+ ```text
+ ```text
+ ```text
+ ```text
+ Gateway install failed: launchctl bootstrap failed: Bootstrap failed: 5: Input/output error
+ ...
+ [gateway] http server listening
+ [gateway] ready
+ [gateway] signal SIGTERM received
+ macOS launchd state showed a submitted updater job named like `ai.openclaw.update.<tag>` repeatedly running a temp update script, with a high run count and `last exit code = 127`. After that submitted updater job exited, launchd signaled the gateway. Removing the submitted updater job and restarting OpenClaw restored a stable beta 8 gateway.
+ Expected behavior: the updater should not leave a keepalive submitted updater job that can repeatedly terminate the gateway. If such a job exists, `openclaw gateway status --deep` or `openclaw doctor` should detect and report it as an actionable cause of a restart loop.
+ Likely source area:
+ Likely source area:
+ Likely source area:
+ - `src/cli/update-cli/update-command.ts`
+ - launchd update/restart helper code
+ - `src/daemon/launchd.ts`
+ - `src/daemon/launchd.ts`
+ - `src/daemon/launchd.ts`
+ ### 2. macOS LaunchAgent env-wrapper path can be blocked or destabilize service refresh
+ The same host showed macOS policy/background-task-management logs against the generated wrapper path under the user's OpenClaw state directory, while the foreground gateway command worked when run directly.
+ AppleSystemPolicy: security policy would not allow process .../.openclaw/service-env/ai.openclaw.gateway-env-wrapper.sh
+ BackgroundTaskManagement: exceeded max notifications for ai.openclaw.gateway-env-wrapper.sh
+ Beta 8 can parse/render `EnvironmentVariables` in launchd plists, but the installer still writes an env-wrapper script whenever service environment entries exist. Rewriting the service to direct Node `ProgramArguments` plus inline `EnvironmentVariables` was enough to make the gateway stable after the stale updater job was removed.
+ Expected behavior: gateway install/refresh on macOS should prefer a stable launchd form that avoids wrapper execution policy problems, or should make wrapper policy failures explicit. Inline `EnvironmentVariables` may be safer for non-secret service env, while secret handling still needs care.
+ - `src/daemon/launchd-plist.ts`
+ - service environment rendering and install/refresh tests
+ ### 3. Gateway service reinstall/refresh can drop local overlay token state
+ During repair, a forced gateway service reinstall wrote the generated service wrapper/env path but did not preserve the local overlay environment token that had previously been present. The result was a gateway that could listen locally but was not authorized for CLI/admin access until token state was restored. Token values are intentionally omitted.
+ Expected behavior: service refresh/reinstall should either preserve local overlay token state, migrate it into the supported launchd environment representation, or fail with a clear message explaining that operator re-auth/re-token setup is required.
+ - service env/local overlay handling
+ - gateway auth token source reconciliation
+ ### 4. Stale updater-process version warning still reproduces on beta 4 to beta 8
+ The stale updater-process warning previously tracked in `openclaw/openclaw#81394` still reproduced on the host updated from beta 4 to beta 8:
+ Restarting service...
+ Your OpenClaw config was written by version 2026.5.12-beta.8, but this command is running 2026.5.12-beta.4.
+ Gateway already reports the updated version after service refresh; skipped redundant restart.
+ The beta 5 to beta 8 host did not show this warning in this run. The host with the launchd failure did not complete the normal restart path, so it is not a clean data point for this specific issue.
+ Expected behavior remains the same as earlier reports: a successful package-manager update should not present known parent-process staleness like an unexpected operator PATH/config mismatch.
+ ### 5. `lossless-claw` stale config and plugin-doctor ambiguity persist
+ One host still carries stale `lossless-claw` config after the earlier security-scanner block:
+ Config warnings:
+ - plugins.entries.lossless-claw: plugin not found: lossless-claw
+ - plugins.allow: plugin not found: lossless-claw
+ On that host, `openclaw plugins doctor` prints those config warnings and then ends with `No plugin issues detected.` On the hosts where `lossless-claw` remains installed, the runtime deprecation warning is now attributed to the plugin/source path, which is an improvement, but the stale-config/final-success ambiguity remains.
+ Expected behavior: `plugins doctor` should either include stale plugin config and missing slot references as findings, or clearly state that its final success line only covers install-tree health.
+ ## Additional Operator Notes
+ These were not treated as beta 8 update regressions:
+ - Existing task-audit old/lost/delivery warnings remained on multiple hosts.
+ - One host still has a pre-existing gateway token source conflict warning.
+ - One host still has optional model-pricing fetch warnings.
+ - The repaired host's remaining direct-model problem is an expired Codex/OpenAI OAuth token and should be handled as a re-authentication task unless maintainers believe fallback behavior should be more visible.
+ ## PR Candidates For A Non-Engineer Using Codex/Claude
+ 1. Add detection/reporting for stale submitted `ai.openclaw.update.*` launchd jobs in `gateway status --deep` or `doctor`, with a targeted test and remediation text.
+ 2. Improve LaunchAgent service env rendering so update/install can use direct Node `ProgramArguments` plus launchd `EnvironmentVariables` where appropriate, or at least reports wrapper policy failures clearly.
+ 3. Make gateway service refresh preserve or explicitly migrate local overlay token state, and fail loudly if auth token state would be lost.

### openclaw-v2026.5.12-self-update-audit-2026-05-14.md  [docs]
+ # OpenClaw v2026.5.12 self-update audit, 2026-05-14
+ ## Scope
+ Three macOS LaunchAgent-backed OpenClaw instances were asked to update themselves to `v2026.5.12` from inside OpenClaw/agent conversations. This report is sanitized: hosts are referred to as Host A, Host B, and Host C, and no private addresses, tokens, local usernames, or machine names are included.
+ ## Outcome
+ | Host | State after user-initiated self-update | Manual repair | Final state |
+ | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+ | Host A | CLI package reached `2026.5.12`, but the gateway LaunchAgent was installed and not loaded. Gateway connectivity failed. | `openclaw gateway restart` re-bootstrapped launchd. | `2026.5.12`, LaunchAgent loaded, gateway reachable, channels connected. |
+ | Host B | Stayed on `2026.5.12-beta.8`; update still available. Gateway LaunchAgent was installed and not loaded. | Ran `openclaw update --tag 2026.5.12 --yes --timeout 1800` outside the gateway via SSH. | `2026.5.12`, LaunchAgent loaded, gateway reachable, Discord connected. |
+ | Host C | Already reached `2026.5.12` and gateway stayed healthy. | None required. | `2026.5.12`, LaunchAgent loaded, gateway reachable, channels connected. |
+ ## Evidence
+ Host A after the failed self-update:
+ ```text
+ ```text
+ ```text
+ ```text
+ ```text
+ ```text
+ OpenClaw 2026.5.12 (f066dd2)
+ Service: LaunchAgent (not loaded)
+ Service: LaunchAgent (not loaded)
+ Connectivity probe: failed
+ Connectivity probe: failed
+ LaunchAgent plist exists but launchd has no loaded job.
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ ```
+ Host A repair:
+ Gateway LaunchAgent was installed but not loaded; re-bootstrapped launchd service.
+ CLI version: 2026.5.12
+ CLI version: 2026.5.12
+ Gateway version: 2026.5.12
+ Gateway version: 2026.5.12
+ Runtime: running
+ Connectivity probe: ok
+ Connectivity probe: ok
+ Host B before repair:
+ OpenClaw 2026.5.12-beta.8 (097daf9)
+ Update: available · pnpm · npm update 2026.5.12
+ Host B manual update:
+ Update Result: OK
+ Before: 2026.5.12-beta.8
+ After: 2026.5.12
+ Restarting service...
+ Gateway already reports the updated version after service refresh; skipped redundant restart.
+ All hosts final verification:
+ Service: LaunchAgent (loaded)
+ Capability: admin-capable
+ ## Diagnosis
+ The failure appears tied to running an update from inside the OpenClaw-managed agent/gateway path. The updater has to stop or refresh the same gateway that is supervising the user-visible agent conversation. In this run, that left one host with the package successfully upgraded but launchd no longer supervising the service, and a second host still on the prior beta with the service not loaded. Running the update from outside the gateway via SSH completed reliably.
+ The issue is related to prior macOS LaunchAgent/update handoff bugs, but this case is specifically about the user-facing self-update workflow: "ask the agent to update itself" can leave the agent offline or not updated, without a durable completion signal for a non-engineer operator.
+ ## Secondary observations
+ - Host B still has stale `lossless-claw` plugin config entries. The stable gateway ignores them, but `openclaw gateway status --deep` repeats warnings:
+ plugins.entries.lossless-claw: plugin not found: lossless-claw
+ plugins.allow: plugin not found: lossless-claw
+ - Host A had unrelated `openai-codex` OAuth refresh failures during earlier smoke testing. That explains some agent-run failures, but not the LaunchAgent unloaded state after the package update.
+ ## Suggested maintainer fixes
+ 1. Detect when `openclaw update` is invoked from inside a managed gateway/agent session and either refuse with a clear handoff command or schedule the update into a detached supervisor process.
+ 2. Make the final update health check fail if the package version changed but the LaunchAgent is installed and not loaded, and print or perform the same re-bootstrap path used by `openclaw gateway restart`.
+ 3. Add an explicit "self-update completed, service loaded, gateway reachable" confirmation that can survive the gateway restart and be delivered back to the initiating channel.
+ 4. Add a regression test or integration harness for macOS LaunchAgent self-update handoff: beta-to-stable update, service stop/restart, launchd load state, and gateway reachability.
+ ## Operator workaround
+ Until this is fixed, avoid asking an OpenClaw agent to update the OpenClaw process that is running it. Update from an outside shell/SSH session instead, then verify:
+ ```bash
+ ```bash
+ openclaw update --tag 2026.5.12 --yes --timeout 1800
+ openclaw gateway status --deep
+ openclaw gateway status --deep
+ openclaw channels status --deep
+ If the package version is current but the gateway is unreachable:
+ openclaw gateway restart

### references/failure-patterns.md  [docs]
+ Symptom:
+ What to inspect:
+ - `openclaw status --deep`
+ Why it matters:
+ ## 33. Discord offline because the managed gateway service is installed but unloaded
+ - Discord shows the bot offline, and local channel status can only report config because the gateway is unreachable
+ - `openclaw doctor` reports `Gateway not running` and a managed service such as a LaunchAgent installed but not loaded
+ - `openclaw update status` may still work from SSH because it does not require the live gateway
+ Observed recovery:
+ - From an outside SSH shell, export the real package-manager path first
+ - Run the requested stable update explicitly, for example `openclaw update --channel stable --yes --timeout 1800`
+ - Re-run `openclaw status --deep` and `openclaw channels status --deep`
+ - A healthy recovery shows the service loaded/running, gateway reachable, the selected channel persisted, and Discord `running, connected`
+ - `command -v openclaw` and `openclaw --version`
+ - `openclaw update status`
+ - `openclaw doctor --non-interactive --no-workspace-suggestions`
+ - `openclaw channels status --deep`
+ - a channel outage can be a service-manager state problem rather than a Discord plugin problem
+ - updating from outside the OpenClaw-managed agent path can recover an unloaded gateway and move the host back to the intended stable channel in one pass
+ - record pre-update warnings separately from the package update result, especially plaintext-secret warnings, stale session metadata, and old task-ledger warnings
+ Remote access guardrail:
+ - If another host cannot be reached over SSH with a short timeout, including from an available jump host, classify it as a transport/access blocker
+ - Do not file an OpenClaw issue for an unreachable host unless you have logs or command output proving OpenClaw failed on that host

